  {
    "id": "d14326879c1e5b370556733000a76789d2778110",
    "individual_note": false,
    "resolvable": true,
    "resolved": true,
    "notes": [
      {
        "id": 3933393912,
        "type": "DiffNote",
        "body": "[P1] Revalidate consent for the hull actually rammed\n\nAt speed 6 or more, lock an unowned NPC hull and issue `shipram` while it is still more than one room away, then use `shiplock` to select a nearby player-owned hull whose owner is offline or has PvP disabled. `vessel_lock_contact()` changes `lock_target` without checking PvP consent or clearing `ramming`, and this tick passes the new target directly to `vessel_ram()`. The consent check in `do_shipram()` therefore protects only the original target: a normal player can damage or sink a protected player's ship. Bind the armed ram to the authorized actor and target, and cancel or revalidate consent when the lock changes and before resolving the impact.\n\nReviewed commit: `648dd94516c9791dcf9cd26ea152768de7ec2075`. Validation: pinned static source review; build, database migrations, and live game tests were not run.",
        "author": {
          "id": 42759441,
          "username": "max757",
          "public_email": "",
          "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
          "state": "active",
          "locked": false,
          "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3c7c169343bd7d0f4575137ce8065aee7cb44024d447bbfe66d773133a81c43e?s=80&d=identicon",
          "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/max757"
        },
        "created_at": "2026-09-30T20:22:46.261Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-09-30T22:20:08.607Z",
