      {
        "id": 3933898943,
        "type": "DiffNote",
        "body": "Fixed in 64c0b4884.\n\n`shipram` now records who gave the order: `ram_order` replaces the `ramming` flag. When the braced hull comes within a room of her contact, `vessel_ram_tick_one()` looks that player up and runs `vessel_fire_permitted()` against the hull locked at that moment. If the player is offline or fails that check, the crew stands down without striking. A relock after bracing is therefore judged at the impact against the new target.\n\n`Test_vessel_ram_tick_rams_the_locked_contact` covers three cases:\n- A relock onto an absent owner's hull: no damage and no cooldown.\n- The NPC hull: the ram strikes.\n- The order's giver leaving the game: the crew stands down.\n\nThe SHIPRAM help and `VESSEL_SYSTEM.md` describe the rule.",
        "author": {
          "id": 42759441,
          "username": "max757",
          "public_email": "",
          "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
          "state": "active",
          "locked": false,
          "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3c7c169343bd7d0f4575137ce8065aee7cb44024d447bbfe66d773133a81c43e?s=80&d=identicon",
