      {
        "id": 3933394125,
        "type": "DiffNote",
        "body": "[P2] Retire existing raiders before deleting their tier mappings\n\nRun this rollback while a Corsair hull still has a `ship_runtime_state` row. This deletion removes its entry from `vessel_raider_tiers`, while the later `NOT EXISTS` guard deliberately retains its prototype because the hull is persisted. On restart, `vessel_raider_boot()` identifies raiders solely through `SELECT DISTINCT prototype_id FROM vessel_raider_tiers`, so it cannot find or retire that hull. Since `raider_mode` is runtime-only, the restored hull also loses its raider despawn and capture restrictions and remains an ordinary public hull, contrary to the rollback's promised restart cleanup. Retire the affected live and persisted hulls before removing the mappings, or retain a durable retirement marker until boot cleanup has completed.\n\nReviewed commit: `648dd94516c9791dcf9cd26ea152768de7ec2075`. Validation: pinned static source review; build, database migrations, and live game tests were not run.",
        "author": {
          "id": 42759441,
          "username": "max757",
          "public_email": "",
          "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
          "state": "active",
          "locked": false,
