      {
        "id": 3933899071,
        "type": "DiffNote",
        "body": "Fixed in a6b17da0f.\n\nThe tier deletion now has the same persisted-hull guard as the prototype deletion. A Corsair prototype with a `ship_runtime_state` row keeps its tier rows, so the restart's `vessel_raider_boot()` still finds and retires her. Rerunning the rollback afterwards removes what was kept. The Phase 22 rollback's comment now says to finish that before dropping the table.\n\nChecked on the test database:\n- With a Corsair Frigate sailing, the rollback kept her prototype and tier row and removed the other five prototypes with their rows.\n- Once her runtime row was gone, a rerun cleared both.\n- The content then reapplied to six prototypes and ten tier rows.",
