      {
        "id": 3933900632,
        "type": null,
        "body": "Both review findings are fixed. The fixes sit on top of the `vessels-s6` tag, one commit each:\n\n- 64c0b4884: a braced ram is tied to the player who ordered it, and consent is checked again at the impact against the hull locked at that moment (P1).\n- a6b17da0f: the raider content rollback keeps a sailing raider's tier rows, so the restart still retires her (P2).\n- 8a7473f01: records the review in `docs/ongoing-projects/vessels-ships.md`.\n\nVerification on `a6b17da0f`:\n- `make test-all` with the database cases on: 1,955 CuTest cases and the protocol harness.\n- The rollback, checked on the test database both with a raider sailing and without.\n- The vessel help verifier.\n- The raider live gate: 182 s.\n- The local CI matrix: all 33 jobs.\n\nReady to merge with a merge commit. Squash stays off, because the study records cite commit hashes.",
